   "daf": "23b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "וְהַקַּרְקָעוֹת תִּשְׁעָה וְכֹהֵן, וְאָדָם כַּיּוֹצֵא בָּהֶן (וְכוּ׳). מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי?",
   "en": "§ If one consecrated «land» and now wishes to redeem it, the land must be assessed by «nine» Israelites «and one priest,» for a total of ten. «And similarly,» assessing the value of «a person» who has pledged his own value to the Temple must be undertaken by ten people, one of whom must be a priest. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters,» that consecrated land must be assessed by ten people, one of whom is a priest, derived?"
  }
